  "name": "QIDI X-Plus 3 / X-Max 3 / X-Smart 3 / Q1 Pro stock toolhead (front 5015 blower with wrap-around duct, right-side inductive probe)",
  "provenance": "QIDI X-Plus 3 / X-Max 3 / X-Smart 3 / Q1 Pro stock toolhead (front 5015 blower with wrap-around duct, right-side inductive probe) Confidence: medium. Sources: https://www.printables.com/model/1420517 (file \"Q1P - Custom toolhead assembly.step\": sub-assemblies \"Stock Toolhead Parts\" and \"QD3.0 Hotend Nozzle Sock\" = stock Q1 Pro geometry, nozzle tip at origin, Z up, -Y front); https://github.com/QIDITECH/QIDI_Q1_Pro/blob/main/config/printer.cfg ([smart_effector] x_offset 17.6 y_offset 4.4; CAD probe centre is exactly (17.6, 4.4), which confirms the CAD frame); https://github.com/ademuri/xplus3/blob/main/printer.cfg (X-Plus 3 [probe] x_offset 27.8 y_offset 6.75); https://www.printables.com/model/1005089 (copy of the X-Smart/Plus/Max 3 stock duct: 54.8 x 35.5 x 37.9 mm, vs Q1 Pro CAD duct 55.0 x 40.7 x 37.5 mm); https://3dprintbeginner.com/qidi-q1-pro-review/ (X axis on 10 mm hollow steel shafts, not a linear rail). The geometry is measured from the Q1 Pro stock parts in the STEP assembly of Printables 1420517. Only the \"Stock Toolhead Parts\" and \"QD3.0 Hotend Nozzle Sock\" sub-assemblies were used; the mod parts (custom covers and duct, GDSTIME fan, Eddy internals) were excluded. Lowest edges above the tip: nozzle 0, inductive probe 1.7, silicone sock 2.3 (10 mm dia bottom, 15 mm above z=4), duct outlet ring 2.41, heatsink and 2510 fan 28.4, X-carriage mounts 33.9. Each level z is about 0.3 mm below the real edge, and footprints have a 0.3 mm margin. The nozzle cone is measured from the CAD: r=0.7 at z=0.1, r=1.8 at z=1.4, then the hex (r=4) from z=2.75. The X-Plus/X-Max/X-Smart 3 share the duct and toolhead layout: the stock duct copy matches within about 1 mm. Their probe sits at x+27.8/y+6.75 (Q1 Pro: 17.6/4.4). The probe body and clamp were translated there and unioned, so xmax (34.1 at z 1.4, 38.5 above) comes from the X-series probe. Probe bottom height 1.7 mm is taken from the Q1 Pro CAD for all four models; it is the user-adjustable inductive sensor. Probing: Q1 Pro and the X-series 3 use an inductive proximity probe for the mesh (Klipper section [smart_effector] on Q1 Pro, [probe] on X-Plus 3); the Q1 Pro sets Z offset with bed-side sensing. Gantry: X runs on two 10 mm steel shafts clamped between \"toolhead mount front\" and \"toolhead mount back\". The lower shaft bearing pocket in the CAD is centred at z~47, y~24 with r~7, so the gantry level is the pocket bottom (40) minus 0.3 margin. The upper shaft is at z~100. Belt clamps protrude to y 41 at z 40-48 and 96-104. The head is 62.4 mm wide (x +/-31.2) and 124 mm tall. Footnote: the X-series 3 hotend (non-QD) sock bottom is assumed equal to the Q1 Pro value (2.3 mm). The bundled qidi_xseries_gen3_hotend.stl preview (15 mm block on a 3 mm stub) agrees within about 0.7 mm. parts: one unmargined box per component, using real lowest edges from the CAD; the consumer adds its own margin. The duct is a U shape: left and right outlet arms with flat bottoms at 2.41, a front bridge at 5.9 and a front lip stepping 3.7 to 4.5. The duct body is split into 6-12, 12-25 and 25-40 mm steps. X-series 3 probe parts are derived and widened 1 mm. The levels and slab_profile keep the 0.3 mm margin. Nozzle: land radius 0.60 mm, 42.0-degree cone to Z=1.50, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 39.70 mm above the tip, Y 16.5..31.5, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/qidi-xseries-gen3.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
